/-
# Problem Description

Stacks Tag 0GSU (Lemma 15.98.3), in the section "Perfect complexes and the eta
operator" of the chapter "More on Algebra".

Throughout, all rings are commutative with unit. For a ring `A`, an element
`f ∈ A` is a *nonzerodivisor* if `f x = 0` implies `x = 0` for all `x ∈ A`.

We work with a *bounded complex of finite free modules*: a cochain complex
`M^• = (M^i, d^i)` of `A`-modules indexed by `i ∈ ℤ` such that each `M^i` is a
finite free `A`-module (`M^i ≅ A^{r_i}` with `r_i = rank_A(M^i) ≥ 0`),
`M^i = 0` for all but finitely many `i` (boundedness), and
`d^i : M^i → M^{i+1}` is `A`-linear with `d^{i+1} ∘ d^i = 0`.

After choosing bases, a complex of finite free modules is recorded by its ranks
`r_i` and, for each `i`, the matrix of `d^i : M^i → M^{i+1}`, namely an
`r_{i+1} × r_i` matrix over `A`. The cochain condition `d^{i+1} ∘ d^i = 0`
becomes the matrix identity `D_{i+1} ⬝ D_i = 0`.

Definition 1 (the map `(f, d^i)`). For `f ∈ A`, the `A`-linear map
`(f, d^i) : M^i → M^i ⊕ M^{i+1}`, `x ↦ (f x, d^i(x))`, is represented (after
choosing bases) by an `(r_i + r_{i+1}) × r_i` matrix: the first `r_i` rows being
`f ⬝ Id_{r_i}` and the remaining `r_{i+1}` rows being the matrix of `d^i`.

Definition 2 (the `r × r` minors and the ideal `I_i`). For an `m × n` matrix `T`
and `r ≥ 0`, an `r × r` minor of `T` is the determinant of an `r × r` submatrix
obtained by selecting `r` rows and `r` columns (a `0 × 0` minor is `1`, and there
are no `r × r` minors when `r > min(m,n)`). For `f` a nonzerodivisor,
`I_i(M^•, f)` is the ideal generated by the `r_i × r_i` minors of the matrix of
`(f, d^i)`. (Independent of bases; note `f^{r_i} ∈ I_i(M^•, f)`.)

Definition 3 (base change). For a ring map `φ : A → B`, the base change
`M^• ⊗_A B` is the complex with terms `M^i ⊗_A B ≅ B^{r_i}` (same ranks) and
differentials `d^i ⊗ id_B` (matrices obtained by applying `φ` entrywise). If
`g = φ(f)` is a nonzerodivisor in `B`, then `I_i(M^• ⊗_A B, g)` is formed as in
Definition 2 over `B`.

Notation. For an ideal `𝔞 ⊆ A` and a ring map `φ : A → B`, `𝔞 B` denotes the
extension `Ideal.map φ 𝔞`.

# Main Statement

Theorem (Stacks Tag 0GSU). Let `φ : A → B` be a ring map, `f ∈ A` a
nonzerodivisor, `M^•` a bounded complex of finite free `A`-modules, and assume
`g := φ(f)` is a nonzerodivisor in `B`. Then for every `i ∈ ℤ`,
`I_i(M^•, f) ⬝ B = I_i(M^• ⊗_A B, g)` as ideals of `B`.
-/

open Matrix

-- Main Definition(s)

/-- The `(r_i + r_{i+1}) × r_i` matrix of the map `(f, d^i) : M^i → M^i ⊕ M^{i+1}`,
`x ↦ (f x, d^i x)`. Rows are indexed by `Fin r_i ⊕ Fin r_{i+1}`: the `Fin r_i`
rows form the block `f • Id_{r_i}` and the `Fin r_{i+1}` rows form the matrix of
`d^i`; columns are indexed by `Fin r_i`. -/
noncomputable def mapMatrix {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {ri ri1 : ℕ}
    (f : A) (d : Matrix (Fin ri1) (Fin ri) A) :
    Matrix (Fin ri ⊕ Fin ri1) (Fin ri) A :=
  Matrix.of fun row col =>
    match row with
    | Sum.inl j => (f • (1 : Matrix (Fin ri) (Fin ri) A)) j col
    | Sum.inr j => d j col

/-- The ideal of `r × r` minors of an `m × n` matrix `T`: the ideal generated by
the determinants of all `r × r` submatrices, where a submatrix is obtained by
selecting `r` rows (an injective `Fin r → m`) and `r` columns (an injective
`Fin r → n`). For `r = 0` the only minor is the determinant of the empty matrix,
which is `1`, so the ideal is the whole ring. For `r > min(m, n)` there are no
injective choices, so the ideal is `0` (the span of the empty set). -/
def minorIdealInjective {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {m n : Type*}
    (T : Matrix m n A) (r : ℕ) : Ideal A :=
  Ideal.span { x : A | ∃ (ri : Fin r → m) (ci : Fin r → n),
    Function.Injective ri ∧ Function.Injective ci ∧ x = (T.submatrix ri ci).det }

/-- A bounded complex of finite free modules over a commutative ring `A`, recorded
after choosing bases by its ranks `rank i = r_i` and the matrices `d i` of its
differentials `d^i : M^i → M^{i+1}` (an `r_{i+1} × r_i` matrix). The field `dd`
records the cochain condition `d^{i+1} ∘ d^i = 0` and `bounded` records that only
finitely many `M^i` are nonzero. -/
@[sga "4½ Rapport 4.11"]
structure BoundedComplex (A : Type*) [CommRing A] where
  /-- The rank `r_i` of the `i`-th term `M^i ≅ A^{r_i}`. -/
  rank : ℤ → ℕ
  /-- The matrix of the differential `d^i : M^i → M^{i+1}`. -/
  d : (i : ℤ) → Matrix (Fin (rank (i+1))) (Fin (rank i)) A
  /-- The cochain condition `d^{i+1} ∘ d^i = 0`. -/
  dd : ∀ i : ℤ, (d (i+1)) * (d i) = 0
  /-- Boundedness: `M^i = 0` (i.e. `r_i = 0`) for all but finitely many `i`. -/
  bounded : {i : ℤ | rank i ≠ 0}.Finite

/-- The ideal `I_i(M^•, f)` generated by the `r_i × r_i` minors of the matrix of
`(f, d^i) : M^i → M^i ⊕ M^{i+1}`. -/
noncomputable def idealI {A : Type*} [CommRing A] (C : BoundedComplex A) (f : A) (i : ℤ) :
    Ideal A :=
  minorIdealInjective (mapMatrix f (C.d i)) (C.rank i)

/-- Base change `M^• ⊗_A B` of a bounded complex of finite free modules along a
ring map `φ : A → B`. The ranks are unchanged and each differential matrix has
`φ` applied entrywise (`d^i ⊗ id_B`). -/
@[ega "III 7.4.1" "special case"]
noncomputable def BoundedComplex.baseChange {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    (C : BoundedComplex A) (φ : A →+* B) : BoundedComplex B where
  rank := C.rank
  d := fun i => (C.d i).map φ
  dd := by
    intro i
    rw [← Matrix.map_mul, C.dd i]
    ext a b
    simp
  bounded := C.bounded

-- Main Statement(s)

/-- **Stacks Tag 0GSU (Lemma 15.98.3).** Let `φ : A → B` be a ring map, `f` a
nonzerodivisor in `A`, `C = M^•` a bounded complex of finite free `A`-modules,
and assume `g = φ(f)` is a nonzerodivisor in `B`. Then for every `i ∈ ℤ`, the
extension of `I_i(M^•, f)` along `φ` equals `I_i(M^• ⊗_A B, g)`. -/
@[stacks 0GSU]
theorem map_idealI_eq_idealI_baseChange {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B)
    (f : A) (C : BoundedComplex A) (i : ℤ) :
    Ideal.map φ (idealI C f i) = idealI (C.baseChange φ) (φ f) i := by
  -- The matrix of `(g, d^i ⊗ id)` is the entrywise image of the matrix of `(f, d^i)`.
  have hmap : mapMatrix (φ f) ((C.baseChange φ).d i) =
      (mapMatrix f (C.d i)).map φ := by
    ext row col
    cases row with
    | inl j =>
        simp only [mapMatrix, BoundedComplex.baseChange, Matrix.of_apply, Matrix.map_apply,
          Matrix.smul_apply, Matrix.one_apply, smul_eq_mul, mul_ite, mul_one, mul_zero,
          apply_ite φ, map_zero]
    | inr j =>
        simp only [mapMatrix, BoundedComplex.baseChange, Matrix.of_apply, Matrix.map_apply]
  unfold idealI minorIdealInjective
  rw [hmap, Ideal.map_span]
  congr 1
  ext x
  have hdet : ∀ {r : ℕ} (ri : Fin r → _) (ci : Fin r → _),
      φ ((mapMatrix f (C.d i)).submatrix ri ci).det =
        (((mapMatrix f (C.d i)).map φ).submatrix ri ci).det :=
    fun ri ci => RingHom.map_det φ _
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨y, ⟨ri, ci, hri, hci, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨ri, ci, hri, hci, hdet ri ci⟩
  · rintro ⟨ri, ci, hri, hci, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨_, ⟨ri, ci, hri, hci, rfl⟩, hdet ri ci⟩

